cartridge "JUNGLE JAKE/C. M. BLAKEMORE/1988"

' JUNGLE JAKE
' A ColecoVision game based on "Jungle Jake" by Cleveland M. Blakemore,
' Ahoy! January 1988 (Commodore 128 BASIC 7.0 with a small machine-language
' interrupt routine for the joystick; disk ahoy1988-01, file JUNGLE JAKE;
' the author from the program's title screen). orig/ has the program, its
' detokenized listing and its sprites. Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI
' made by Anthropic), 2026, in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' Not a line-by-line port: the rules are the original's (read from its
' listing; the C-128 program does not run in this toolbox's C-64
' emulator), the game is built for the ColecoVision: smooth 16 x 16
' sprites, a two-colour Jake with walking, jumping and climbing frames,
' tiled jungle floors, roots, ferns, trunks and vines, sound effects and
' an original title tune.
'
' The game: Jake's friend hangs in a cage at the top left of the jungle.
' Four floors are joined by vines at alternate ends: walk right along the
' bottom floor to the vine at the right end, left along the second to the
' vine at the left, right along the third, then left along the top floor
' and jump up to the cage. Reaching the end of a floor climbs its vine by
' itself. Five pests roam each level, and touching one costs a life:
'   1 BITE IN THE ASP       asps, one a floor (two on top), left and right
'   2 FOR THE BIRDS         birds flying any way over the whole jungle
'   3 WARTHOG COUNTRY       slow warthogs on the floors
'   4 MONKEY BUSINESS       monkeys going up and down five long vines
'   5 SNAKE YOUR BODY       snakes on the floors
'   6 PECKERS FROM ABOVE    birds diving up and down in five lanes
'   7 BIG CAT HEAVEN!       big cats on the floors
' Each pest is still until it is first sent off; then, as in the original,
' one pest at a time is given a new random direction (a few times a
' second), so the floors' pests wander back and forth and go round the
' screen's edges. A climbed vine scores 100 x level x the floor reached; a
' freed friend 1000 x level. Four lives; a lost life starts the level again
' from the bottom. Free the friend on all seven levels to be the JUNGLE JAKE
' CHAMPION.
'
' From the original (orig/junglejake.bas): the four floors and their vines
' (right, left, right), the climb when Jake reaches a floor's end not
' jumping, the cage at the top left reached by a jump, Jake's walk at a
' pixel a frame (its machine code moved him a pixel an interrupt) with the
' stick working during a jump, a jump held as long as the button is held,
' the seven levels' pests, speeds (MOVSPR 2, 2, 1, 3, 2, 2, 2), starting
' places (the middle of each floor and two on the top; the birds together
' at the top; the up-and-down lanes 48 C-128 pixels apart) and kinds of
' motion (left/right, any angle, up/down), the pests starting still, one
' random pest redirected each pass, the floor-walkers going round the
' screen's edges (the C-128 moved sprites over 512 x positions, about 170
' of them off screen), the up-and-down and flying pests stopped at the top
' and the bottom of the jungle (its interrupt clamped every sprite between
' Y 48 and 222), touching while climbing still counts, the level colours
' of the floors, the scores, four lives, the level pages with their names,
' CONGRATULATIONS / JUNGLE JAKE CHAMPION! after level 7, the high score.
'
' Liberties: the warriors of level 3 and the headshrinkers of level 7
' (caricatures of African people) are warthogs and big cats here; the
' captive in a cooking pot is Jake's friend in a hanging cage. The screen
' is 0.8 times the C-128's across (its 320 pixels into 256) and the floors
' are 40 pixels apart (48), so the jump is 24 pixels high (28) over 40
' frames, a smooth arc (the C-128's rose 27 and dropped back in about 15
' BASIC passes). Pests are redirected every 12 frames (the C-128 did it
' once a BASIC pass, several times a second); their speeds are 5/16, 1/2
' and 3/4 of a pixel a frame for MOVSPR 1, 2, 3, against Jake's pixel.
' Tuned with a human-paced bot (a stale view of 12 frames, no foreknowledge
' of the turns): at 1/2, 3/4, 1 with turns every 6 frames and a 20-pixel
' jump it never cleared level 1; now eight such games freed the friend on
' 0, 7, 3, 0, 7, 0, 0 and 2 levels, so level 1 is still a real test.
' Flying pests have 16 directions (360). Touching is a box test (the
' C-128 tested sprite pixels), the asp's raised head counting from its
' fifth row. Jake climbs a pixel a frame. Before play starts and after a
' lost life there is a second of GET READY; the pests stand still while
' Jake falls. Six-digit score.
'
' Controls: the joystick (either controller): left and right walk, either
' button jumps (hold it to keep jumping). On the title, up and down
' choose, a button starts.
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128; the
' frame loop is protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI off
' after a wait, display off. Music first in the sound table, effects after;
' the title tune is played once. `set sprite count` is always given.
' Nothing flashes.

const TGround0 = 128
const TGround1 = 129
const TGround2 = 130
const TGround3 = 131
const TGround4 = 132
const TGround5 = 133
const TGround6 = 134
const TEarth = 135
const TRootsa = 136
const TRootsb = 137
const TFerna = 138
const TFernb = 139
const TLeafa = 140
const TLeafb = 141
const TTrunk = 142
const TVinel = 143
const TViner = 144
const TMvine = 145
const TBranch = 146
const TBranchend = 147
const TRope = 148
const TMan = 149
const TSkull00 = 150
const TSkull01 = 151
const TSkull10 = 152
const TSkull11 = 153
const TLgj00 = 154
const TLgj01 = 155
const TLgj10 = 156
const TLgj11 = 157
const TLgu00 = 158
const TLgu01 = 159
const TLgu10 = 160
const TLgu11 = 161
const TLgn00 = 162
const TLgn01 = 163
const TLgn10 = 164
const TLgn11 = 165
const TLgg00 = 166
const TLgg01 = 167
const TLgg10 = 168
const TLgg11 = 169
const TLgl00 = 170
const TLgl01 = 171
const TLgl10 = 172
const TLgl11 = 173
const TLge00 = 174
const TLge01 = 175
const TLge10 = 176
const TLge11 = 177
const TLga00 = 178
const TLga01 = 179
const TLga10 = 180
const TLga11 = 181
const TLgk00 = 182
const TLgk01 = 183
const TLgk10 = 184
const TLgk11 = 185
const SJr0a = 0
const SJr0b = 4
const SJr1a = 8
const SJr1b = 12
const SJl0a = 16
const SJl0b = 20
const SJl1a = 24
const SJl1b = 28
const SJc0a = 32
const SJc0b = 36
const SJc1a = 40
const SJc1b = 44
const SJda = 48
const SJdb = 52
const SPal0 = 56
const SPal1 = 60
const SCage = 64
const SAspr0 = 68
const SAspr1 = 72
const SAspl0 = 76
const SAspl1 = 80
const SHogr0 = 84
const SHogr1 = 88
const SHogl0 = 92
const SHogl1 = 96
const SCatr0 = 100
const SCatr1 = 104
const SCatl0 = 108
const SCatl1 = 112
const SSnaker0 = 116
const SSnaker1 = 120
const SSnakel0 = 124
const SSnakel1 = 128
const SBirdr0 = 132
const SBirdr1 = 136
const SBirdl0 = 140
const SBirdl1 = 144
const SPeckr0 = 148
const SPeckr1 = 152
const SPeckl0 = 156
const SPeckl1 = 160
const SMonkr0 = 164
const SMonkr1 = 168
const SMonkl0 = 172
const SMonkl1 = 176
const NTiles8 = 464
const SprBytes = 1440
const JumpN = 40
const SndTuneA = 1
const SndTuneB = 2
const SndJump = 3
const SndStep = 4
const SndClimbed = 5
const SndHit = 6
const SndFall = 7
const SndFree = 8
const SndIntro = 9
const SndStart = 10
const SndOver = 11
const SndWin = 12
const NSpr = 9
const XMin = 16
const XMax = 224
const JakeX0 = 20
const RedirN = 12
const XWrap = 5120
const XSeen = 4096
const YMin16 = 256
const YMax16 = 2560
const MidX16 = 1856
const PalX = 16
const PalY = 18
' states of a pass of play
const StReady = 1
const StPlay = 2
const StClimb = 3
const StHit = 4
const StFree = 5

record Foe:
  i16 X
  i16 Y
  u8 Dir
  u8 Mv
end record

' the floors: Jake's top line standing on each, the tile row
data FloorY bytes
  160,120,80,40
end data
data FloorRow bytes
  22,17,12,7
end data
' the up-and-down lanes (sprite x)
data LaneX bytes
  36,76,116,156,196
end data
' the pests' boxes inside their sprites by level (top and bottom rows)
data FoeTop bytes
  5,2,7,0,10,0,6
end data
data FoeBot bytes
  15,11,14,14,14,13,14
end data

u16 TzLeft = 0
u8 TzOn = 0
Foe Fo[5]
u16 Seed = 4321
' Jake: x, top line, jump frame (0 on the ground), floor, facing (0 right,
' 1 left), animation frame, walk counter
u8 Jx = JakeX0
u8 Jy = 160
u8 Jt = 0
u8 Fl = 0
u8 Face = 0
u8 Frm = 0
u8 Wk = 0
u8 Lv = 0
u8 Men = 4
u8 Rt = 0
u8 PalF = 0
bcd digits 6 Score = 0
bcd digits 6 HiScore = 0
u8 St = StReady
u8 StT = 0
u8 Over = 0
u8 Phase = 0
' input
u8 Pad = 0
u8 Btn = 0
u8 WasBtn = 0
u8 Press = 0
u8 WasStick = 0
u8 Menu = 0
u8 Tick = 0
u8 Idle = 0
u8 Anim = 0
' loop counters (never shared with the helpers)
u8 Ci = 0
u8 Ri = 0
u8 Gi = 0
u8 Si = 0
' scratch
u16 W16 = 0
u16 NumU = 0
u8 J = 0
u8 K = 0
u8 V = 0
u8 X = 0
u8 Y = 0

  tile screen
  set sound table JkSoundTable areas 6
  sprites 16x16
  set sprite count NSpr
  sprites stable 0 to 1
  sprites flicker on
  nmi off
  copy SpritePat count SprBytes to vram.spr_pat
  HideSprites
  screen on
  CreditsPage

title:
  TitlePage
  if Menu = 1 then goto title

new_game:
  NewGame

play_loop:
  Frame1
  ReadPad
  PlayStep
  DrawSprites
  if Over = 0 then goto play_loop

  ' the end: a message, then back to the title on a press
  Phase = 4
  if Score > HiScore then HiScore = Score
  ShowHud
  mute all
  if Over = 2 then
    print at 6,9, "                    "
    print at 6,10, "  CONGRATULATIONS!  "
    print at 6,11, "                    "
    print at 6,12, "JUNGLE JAKE CHAMPION"
    print at 6,13, "                    "
    play sound SndWin
  else
    print at 9,10, "             "
    print at 9,11, "  GAME OVER  "
    print at 9,12, "             "
    play sound SndOver
  end if
  Rearm
  wait 60 frames
  ' a press goes back to the title; left alone, Amy's sleep blanks the
  ' screen after 30 seconds to spare the TV, and a press wakes it
  nmi on
  pause until press and release sleep after 30 seconds
  nmi off
  goto title

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' random numbers: a 16-bit xorshift, stirred on the title

function Rnd as u8
  u8 Lo = 0
  Seed = Seed ^ (Seed << 7)
  Seed = Seed ^ (Seed >> 9)
  Seed = Seed ^ (Seed << 8)
  Lo = Seed & 255
  return Lo

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' one pass of play

sub PlayStep:
  inc Anim
  select case St
  case StReady
    inc StT
    if StT >= 60 then
      St = StPlay
      StT = 0
      ClearMsg
    end if
  case StPlay
    MoveJake
    if St <> StPlay then return
    Redirect
    MoveFoes
    Collide
  case StClimb
    MoveFoes
    ClimbStep
    Collide
  case StHit
    inc StT
    if StT = 20 then play sound SndFall
    if StT >= 120 then LoseMan
  case StFree
    FreeStep
  end select
  return
end sub

' the stick walks (a pixel a frame, in the air too), the button jumps; at
' the end of a floor (not jumping) the vine is climbed
sub MoveJake:
  u8 Moved = 0
  V = Pad & 4
  if V > 0 then
    Face = 1
    if Jx > XMin then
      dec Jx
      Moved = 1
    end if
  else
    V = Pad & 8
    if V > 0 then
      Face = 0
      if Jx < XMax then
        inc Jx
        Moved = 1
      end if
    end if
  end if
  if Moved = 1 then
    inc Wk
    if Jt = 0 then
      V = Wk & 15
      if V = 0 then play sound SndStep
    end if
  end if
  if Jt = 0 then
    V = Pad & 16
    if V > 0 then
      Jt = 1
      play sound SndJump
    end if
  end if
  if Jt > 0 then
    Jy = FloorY[Fl] - JumpT[Jt - 1]
    inc Jt
    if Jt > JumpN then
      Jt = 0
      Jy = FloorY[Fl]
    end if
  end if
  Frm = (Wk >> 3) & 1
  if Jt > 0 then Frm = 1
  if Jt = 0 then
    select case (Fl, Jx)
    case (0, XMax), (2, XMax), (1, XMin)
      St = StClimb
      StT = 0
    end select
  end if
  return
end sub

' up the vine a pixel a frame; at the floor above, its score
sub ClimbStep:
  u8 Goal = 0
  dec Jy
  Frm = (Jy >> 2) & 1
  V = Jy & 7
  if V = 0 then play sound SndStep
  Goal = FloorY[Fl + 1]
  if Jy > Goal then return
  ArriveFloor
  return
end sub

' the floor above reached: 100 x level x floor, facing the next vine
' (its own sub: a return before a FOR with a variable end in the same sub
' is miscompiled, bugs/jake-return-before-for.alexis)
sub ArriveFloor:
  inc Fl
  K = (Lv + 1) * Fl
  for Si = 1 to K
    Score += 100
  next
  ShowScore
  play sound SndClimbed
  if Fl = 1 then
    Face = 1
  else
    Face = 0
  end if
  Frm = 0
  St = StPlay
  return
end sub

' a pest at a time gets a new random direction
sub Redirect:
  u8 Pick = 0
  u8 Rv = 0
  inc Rt
  if Rt < RedirN then return
  Rt = 0
  Pick = Rnd() % 5
  Rv = Rnd()
  select case LvKind[Lv]
  case 0
    Fo[Pick].Dir = (Rv & 1) * 8
  case 1
    Fo[Pick].Dir = Rv & 15
  case else
    Fo[Pick].Dir = 4 + (Rv & 1) * 8
  end select
  Fo[Pick].Mv = 1
  return
end sub

' every pest moving goes its way: round the screen's edges across (320
' pixels around, 64 of them off screen), stopped at the top and the bottom
sub MoveFoes:
  i16 Dx = 0
  i16 Dy = 0
  W16 = Lv * 16
  for Ci = 0 to 4
    if Fo[Ci].Mv = 1 then
      NumU = W16 + Fo[Ci].Dir
      Dx = VxT[NumU]
      Dx = Dx - 64
      Dy = VyT[NumU]
      Dy = Dy - 64
      Fo[Ci].X = Fo[Ci].X + Dx
      if Fo[Ci].X < 0 then Fo[Ci].X = Fo[Ci].X + XWrap
      if Fo[Ci].X >= XWrap then Fo[Ci].X = Fo[Ci].X - XWrap
      Fo[Ci].Y = Fo[Ci].Y + Dy
      if Fo[Ci].Y < YMin16 then Fo[Ci].Y = YMin16
      if Fo[Ci].Y > YMax16 then Fo[Ci].Y = YMax16
    end if
  next
  return
end sub

' touching: the friend first (as the C-128 tested the cage's sprite bit
' first), then the pests
sub Collide:
  if Fl = 3 then
    if Jx <= 24 then
      if Jy <= 29 then
        St = StFree
        StT = 0
        Jt = 0
        return
      end if
    end if
  end if
  for Ci = 0 to 4
    if Touch(Ci) = 1 then
      St = StHit
      StT = 0
      Jt = 0
      play sound SndHit
      return
    end if
  next
  return
end sub

' 1 when pest Which's box meets Jake's (columns 5-10, rows 2-15)
function Touch(u8 Which) as u8
  i16 Fx = 0
  i16 Fy = 0
  i16 A = 0
  i16 B = 0
  if Fo[Which].X >= XSeen then return 0
  Fx = Fo[Which].X >> 4
  Fy = Fo[Which].Y >> 4
  A = Fx + 3
  B = Jx + 10
  if A > B then return 0
  A = Fx + 12
  B = Jx + 5
  if A < B then return 0
  A = Fy + FoeTop[Lv]
  B = Jy + 15
  if A > B then return 0
  A = Fy + FoeBot[Lv]
  B = Jy + 2
  if A < B then return 0
  return 1

' the friend is free: the score, the cheering, then the next level
sub FreeStep:
  inc StT
  if StT = 1 then
    K = Lv + 1
    for Si = 1 to K
      Score += 1000
    next
    ShowScore
    play sound SndFree
  end if
  PalF = (StT >> 3) & 1
  Jy = FloorY[3]
  if StT < 150 then return
  inc Lv
  if Lv >= 7 then
    Lv = 6
    Over = 2
    return
  end if
  StartLevel
  return
end sub

sub LoseMan:
  dec Men
  if Men = 0 then
    Over = 1
    return
  end if
  DrawMen
  ResetLife
  ShowMsg
  return
end sub

' Jake at the bottom left, the pests still at their starting places
sub ResetLife:
  u8 F = 0
  Fl = 0
  Jx = JakeX0
  Jy = FloorY[0]
  Jt = 0
  Face = 0
  Frm = 0
  Wk = 0
  Rt = 0
  PalF = 0
  for Ci = 0 to 4
    Fo[Ci].Mv = 0
    select case LvKind[Lv]
    case 0
      F = Ci
      if F > 3 then F = 3
      Fo[Ci].X = MidX16
      Fo[Ci].Y = FloorY[F] * 16
      Fo[Ci].Dir = 8
    case 1
      Fo[Ci].X = MidX16
      Fo[Ci].Y = YMin16
      Fo[Ci].Dir = 4
    case else
      Fo[Ci].X = LaneX[Ci] * 16
      Fo[Ci].Y = YMin16
      Fo[Ci].Dir = 4
    end select
  next
  St = StReady
  StT = 0
  return
end sub

' a level: its page, then the jungle
sub StartLevel:
  LevelPage
  Phase = 1
  NewScreen
  DrawJungle
  ShowHud
  ResetLife
  ShowMsg
  DrawSprites
  ShowScreen
  play sound SndStart
  return
end sub

sub NewGame:
  Score = 0
  Men = 4
  Lv = 0
  Over = 0
  StartLevel
  return
end sub

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' drawing

' the jungle of level Lv: canopy, the floors in the level's colour, roots,
' ferns, trunks, the climbing vines (and the monkeys' vines), the branch
sub DrawJungle:
  u8 T = 0
  u8 R = 0
  fill TLeafa count 32 at 0,0
  for Gi = 1 to 31 step 2
    put char TLeafb at Gi,0
  next
  fill TBranch count 5 at 0,2
  put char TRope at 2,2
  put char TBranchend at 5,2
  T = TGround0 + Lv
  for Gi = 0 to 3
    R = FloorRow[Gi]
    fill T count 32 at 0,R
    ' roots under the floor, ferns on it
    Y = R + 1
    if Y < 23 then
      for Ri = 0 to 31
        V = (Ri * 5 + Y) & 3
        if V = 0 then put char TRootsa at Ri,Y
        if V = 2 then put char TRootsb at Ri,Y
      next
    end if
    Y = R - 1
    for Ri = 4 to 27
      V = (Ri * 3 + Y) % 7
      if V = 0 then put char TFerna at Ri,Y
      if V = 4 then put char TFernb at Ri,Y
    next
  next
  fill TEarth count 32 at 0,23
  ' trunks (over the roots)
  for Gi = 3 to 6
    put char TTrunk at 22,Gi
  next
  for Gi = 13 to 16
    put char TTrunk at 22,Gi
  next
  for Gi = 8 to 11
    put char TTrunk at 8,Gi
  next
  for Gi = 18 to 21
    put char TTrunk at 8,Gi
  next
  ' the climbing vines: right end (floor 0 to 1), left (1 to 2), right
  for Gi = 18 to 21
    put char TViner at 29,Gi
  next
  for Gi = 13 to 16
    put char TVinel at 2,Gi
  next
  for Gi = 8 to 11
    put char TViner at 29,Gi
  next
  if Lv = 3 then
    for Ri = 0 to 4
      X = LaneX[Ri] + 8
      X = X >> 3
      for Gi = 2 to 21
        select case Gi
        case 7, 12, 17
        case else
          put char TMvine at X,Gi
        end select
      next
    next
  end if
  return
end sub

sub ShowHud:
  fill 32 count 28 at 2,1
  print at 2,1, "SCORE"
  print at 18,1, "HI"
  print HiScore at 21,1
  ShowScore
  NumU = Lv + 1
  print at 8,2, "LEVEL " + digits$(NumU, 1)
  DrawMen
  return
end sub

sub ShowScore:
  print Score at 8,1
  return
end sub

' the lives left, as heads at the right of row 2
sub DrawMen:
  u8 Col = 0
  fill 32 count 8 at 22,2
  if Men > 0 then
    for Gi = 1 to Men
      Col = 31 - Gi * 2
      put char TMan at Col,2
    next
  end if
  return
end sub

sub ShowMsg:
  print at 10,4, " GET READY "
  return
end sub

' row 4 again as it was (the GET READY box)
sub ClearMsg:
  fill 32 count 11 at 10,4
  return
end sub

' sprites: 0-1 Jake (khaki over skin), 2 the cage, 3 the friend, 4-8 the
' pests
sub DrawSprites:
  u8 P = 0
  u8 Sy = 0
  u8 Col = 0
  Sy = Jy - 1
  if St = StHit then
    P = SJda
  elseif St = StClimb then
    P = SJc0a + Frm * 8
  else
    P = SJr0a + Face * 16 + Frm * 8
  end if
  set sprite 0 to Sy,Jx,P,11
  P = P + 4
  set sprite 1 to Sy,Jx,P,9
  if St = StFree then
    set sprite 2 to 192,0,0,0
    P = SPal0 + PalF * 4
  else
    set sprite 2 to PalY - 1,PalX,SCage,10
    P = SPal0
  end if
  set sprite 3 to PalY - 1,PalX,P,15
  Col = LvCol[Lv]
  for Ci = 0 to 4
    J = Ci + 4
    if Fo[Ci].X >= XSeen then
      set sprite J to 192,0,0,0
    else
      P = PestPat(Ci)
      X = Fo[Ci].X >> 4
      Sy = Fo[Ci].Y >> 4
      Sy = Sy - 1
      set sprite J to Sy,X,P,Col
    end if
  next
  update sprites
  return
end sub

' a pest's pattern: its kind, facing (left for directions 5-11, except the
' up-and-down kinds) and stride (still when it has never moved)
function PestPat(u8 Which) as u8
  u8 Pp = 0
  u8 D = 0
  Pp = LvPat[Lv]
  if Fo[Which].Mv = 1 then
    Pp = Pp + (((Anim >> 3) + Which) & 1) * 4
  end if
  if LvKind[Lv] = 2 then return Pp
  D = Fo[Which].Dir
  if D >= 5 then
    if D <= 11 then Pp = Pp + 8
  end if
  return Pp

' the level page: its number and name between two skulls, a jingle
sub LevelPage:
  u8 Nc = 0
  Phase = 2
  NewScreen
  fill TLeafa count 32 at 0,0
  fill TEarth count 32 at 0,23
  NumU = Lv + 1
  print at 12,7, "LEVEL " + digits$(NumU, 1)
  put char TSkull00 at 4,10
  put char TSkull01 at 5,10
  put char TSkull10 at 4,11
  put char TSkull11 at 5,11
  put char TSkull00 at 26,10
  put char TSkull01 at 27,10
  put char TSkull10 at 26,11
  put char TSkull11 at 27,11
  Nc = NameCol(Lv)
  select case Lv
  case 0
    print at Nc,10, "BITE IN THE ASP"
  case 1
    print at Nc,10, "FOR THE BIRDS"
  case 2
    print at Nc,10, "WARTHOG COUNTRY"
  case 3
    print at Nc,10, "MONKEY BUSINESS"
  case 4
    print at Nc,10, "SNAKE YOUR BODY"
  case 5
    print at Nc,10, "PECKERS FROM"
    print at 12,11, "ABOVE"
  case else
    print at Nc,10, "BIG CAT HEAVEN!"
  end select
  print at 9,15, "FREE YOUR FRIEND"
  ShowScreen
  play sound SndIntro
  for Gi = 1 to 150
    Frame1
  next
  return
end sub

' the column that centres a level's name in the 32 columns
function NameCol(u8 L) as u8
  u8 Ln = 15
  if L = 1 then Ln = 13
  if L = 5 then Ln = 12
  return (32 - Ln) >> 1

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sub Rearm:
  if TzOn = 1 then
    dec TzLeft
    if TzLeft = 0 then
      stop sound SndTuneA
      stop sound SndTuneB
      TzOn = 0
    end if
  end if
  nmi off
  nmi on
  return
end sub

sub Frame1:
  Rearm
  Idle = 1
  wait
  Idle = 0
  nmi off
  inc Tick
  return
end sub

sub ReadPad:
  Pad = 0
  if joypad(1).up then Pad = Pad | 1
  if joypad(1).down then Pad = Pad | 2
  if joypad(1).left then Pad = Pad | 4
  if joypad(1).right then Pad = Pad | 8
  if joypad(1).fire then Pad = Pad | 16
  if joypad(2).up then Pad = Pad | 1
  if joypad(2).down then Pad = Pad | 2
  if joypad(2).left then Pad = Pad | 4
  if joypad(2).right then Pad = Pad | 8
  if joypad(2).fire then Pad = Pad | 16
  Btn = Pad & 16
  Press = 0
  if Btn > 0 then
    if WasBtn = 0 then Press = 1
  end if
  WasBtn = Btn
  return
end sub

sub HideSprites:
  clear sprites
  set sprite count NSpr
  for J = 0 to 8
    set sprite J to 192,0,0,0
  next
  update sprites
  return
end sub

sub NewScreen:
  Rearm
  wait
  nmi off
  display off
  HideSprites
  fill mode 2 text color with $F1
  copy TilePat count NTiles8 to vram.pattern + 1024
  copy TileCol count NTiles8 to vram.color + 1024
  copy TilePat count NTiles8 to vram.pattern + 3072
  copy TilePat count NTiles8 to vram.pattern + 5120
  backdrop black
  cls
  return
end sub

sub ShowScreen:
  Rearm
  wait
  nmi off
  screen on
  nmi off
  return
end sub

' the title: the logo, the author, Jake walking on a floor of the jungle,
' the tune once, START / CREDITS
sub TitlePage:
  u8 Code = 0
  u8 Col = 0
  Phase = 5
  NewScreen
  fill TLeafa count 32 at 0,0
  for Gi = 1 to 31 step 2
    put char TLeafb at Gi,0
  next
  ' JUNGLE JAKE in 2 x 2 letters (a space after JUNGLE)
  Col = 5
  for Gi = 0 to 9
    Code = LogoT[Gi]
    put char Code at Col,3
    inc Code
    put char Code at Col + 1,3
    inc Code
    put char Code at Col,4
    inc Code
    put char Code at Col + 1,4
    Col = Col + 2
    if Gi = 5 then Col = Col + 2
  next
  print at 7,7, "AHOY! JANUARY 1988"
  print at 3,8, "BY CLEVELAND M. BLAKEMORE"
  print at 12,11, "  START"
  print at 12,12, "  CREDITS"
  print at 11,20, "HI"
  print HiScore at 14,20
  fill TGround0 count 32 at 0,17
  for Ri = 0 to 31
    V = Ri & 3
    if V = 0 then put char TRootsa at Ri,18
    if V = 2 then put char TRootsb at Ri,18
  next
  put char TFerna at 6,16
  put char TFernb at 25,16
  fill TEarth count 32 at 0,23
  ShowMenu
  ShowScreen
  play sound SndTuneA
  play sound SndTuneB
  TzLeft = 1024
  TzOn = 1
  Jx = 40
  Face = 0
  Wk = 0
  Rearm
  wait no fire
  nmi off
  Phase = 6
tp_loop:
  Frame1
  ReadPad
  V = Rnd()
  ' Jake strolls to and fro
  if Face = 0 then
    inc Jx
    if Jx >= 200 then Face = 1
  else
    dec Jx
    if Jx <= 40 then Face = 0
  end if
  inc Wk
  Frm = (Wk >> 3) & 1
  K = SJr0a + Face * 16 + Frm * 8
  set sprite 0 to 119,Jx,K,11
  K = K + 4
  set sprite 1 to 119,Jx,K,9
  update sprites
  V = Pad & 3
  if V > 0 then
    if WasStick = 0 then
      K = V & 1
      if K > 0 then
        Menu = 0
      else
        Menu = 1
      end if
      ShowMenu
    end if
  end if
  WasStick = V
  if Press = 0 then goto tp_loop
  stop sound SndTuneA
  stop sound SndTuneB
  mute all
  TzOn = 0
  HideSprites
  if Menu = 1 then CreditsPage
  return
end sub

sub ShowMenu:
  put char 32 at 13,11
  put char 32 at 13,12
  J = Menu + 11
  put char 62 at 13,J
  return
end sub

sub CreditsPage:
  Phase = 7
  NewScreen
  print at 10,2, "JUNGLE JAKE"
  print at 2,5, "BASED ON JUNGLE JAKE BY"
  print at 2,6, "CLEVELAND M. BLAKEMORE,"
  print at 2,7, "AHOY! JANUARY 1988"
  print at 2,8, "(COMMODORE 128)."
  print at 2,11, "COLECOVISION GAME, MUSIC"
  print at 2,12, "AND PICTURES BY CLAUDE"
  print at 2,13, "(ANTHROPIC) FOR AMY STUDIO,"
  print at 2,14, "IN AMY BY AMY BIENVENU,"
  print at 2,15, "2026."
  print at 2,18, "MUSIC: VINE SWING"
  print at 2,19, "(ORIGINAL)"
  print at 8,21, "PRESS THE BUTTON"
  ShowScreen
  Phase = 8
  Rearm
  pause until press
  wait no fire
  nmi off
  return
end sub

